WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.574
In this lesson, you will learn to use event hats (flag, key, click, broadcast) to make programs respond to users, and run several scripts at the same time.

2
00:00:14.174 --> 00:00:21.930
Most apps wait for events — a tap, a key, a message — and then react.

3
00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:27.078
In Scratch, hat blocks start scripts when an event happens.

4
00:00:27.678 --> 00:00:31.087
A sprite can have many scripts.

5
00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:37.539
They run at the same time, like several workers each doing one job.

6
00:00:38.139 --> 00:00:41.983
Broadcast sends a message to every sprite.

7
00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:46.696
Any script with “when I receive” that message starts.

8
00:00:46.696 --> 00:00:50.974
This is how sprites talk to each other.

9
00:00:51.574 --> 00:00:56.287
Web pages do the same thing: button.onclick = startParty.

10
00:00:56.287 --> 00:00:58.826
Same idea, different language.

11
00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:03.270
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

12
00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:08.417
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
